# Isolates the collector's cost per list cell. Each round builds a one million
# element integer list whose every cell stays live while it grows, so the
# collections during the build copy cells and little else.
# Read it as: instructions(gc-cells) - instructions(gc-cells-short), divided
# by copied_objects(gc-cells) - copied_objects(gc-cells-short), summed over the
# fz.runtime.gc events.
def build(0, acc), do: acc
def build(n, acc), do: build(n - 1, [n | acc])
def rounds(0, sum), do: sum
def rounds(r, sum) do
  xs = build(1000000, [])
  rounds(r - 1, sum + length(xs))
end
def main(), do: dbg(rounds(10, 0))
